      "explanation": "525. D. The curvature of the Earth causes the sun’s rays to spread out\n     over a larger surface area at the poles compared to at the\n     equator.\n     When the sun’s rays hit the Earth’s surface at an angle (like at the\n     poles), the heat energy from them is spread out over a larger area,\n     making the temperatures cooler there. Hence, Choice (D) is the\n     correct answer. Choices (B) and (C) are false statements. Choice (A)\n     confuses cause with effect. The cold temperatures at the poles cause\n     water to freeze into snow and ice; the snow and ice don’t cool the air.",
