      "explanation": "622. B. The water evaporated, leaving salt behind.\n     Brine contains dissolved salt. When the water boils, the salt gets left\n     behind at the bottom of the pan; the white residue is the salt, making\n     Choice (B) the correct answer.\n     Rust is brown, not white, and would not occur so quickly; therefore,\n     you can reject Choice (A). Water doesn’t burn, so you can also reject\n     Choice (C). There’s no evidence that the pan was dirty, so you can\n     reject Choice (D).",
