      "correctLabel": "A",
      "answerLine": "A. downward",
      "explanation": "623. A. downward\n     According to Newton’s second law, the acceleration of an object (in\n     this case, the elevator) is always in the same direction as the\n     unbalanced force. Because the elevator is initially accelerating\n     downward, the unbalanced force must also be acting downward, so\n     Choice (A) is correct.",
