      "answerLine": "B. 25%",
      "explanation": "658. B. 25%\n     Because the allele for purple flowers, P, is dominant, any genotype\n     that contains it (Pp or PP) will result in purple flowers. The Punnett\n     square shows that three out of four (or 75 percent) of the offspring\n     have genotypes containing the dominant allele; hence, 75 percent of\n     the offspring will have purple flowers. That leaves only one out of\n\n     four (or 25 percent) of the offspring with the recessive (pp) genotype\n     that will result in white flowers, making Choice (B) the correct\n     answer.",
