      "explanation": "818. D. enthusiastic and informative\n     The author’s tone in the passage can best be described as enthusiastic\n     and informative, making Choice (D) the best answer. He is not grim\n     or sardonic (cynical), so you can reject Choice (A). He is not being\n     sarcastic (mocking with contempt), so Choice (B) can be rejected.\n     He is not being disingenuous (pretending to know less about the\n     subject than he actually does), so Choice (C) is incorrect.",
